  "description": "Companion package of Gtk.Windows.Forms. Gives System.Windows.Forms.WebBrowser the legacy Internet Explorer (Trident) engine on Windows by hosting the SHDocVw WebBrowser ActiveX control. It registers below the WebView2 backend, so WebView2 is still preferred when installed and this is the fallback before WebKitGTK. Referencing the package is the whole opt-in - a module initializer registers the backend. Note the airspace limitation: GTK 4 gives only toplevel windows an HWND, so the browser is a child window painted above all GTK content in that window and is not clipped by overlapping widgets, popovers or menus. Internet Explorer is end of life; use this only for legacy intranet content that requires Trident.",
